# Python leaves these beside the vendored engine's own scripts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Written per-machine by commit-identity.sh (it derives TZ from
# identity.json and stores it here), so it is never the same on two
# checkouts and must not be committed.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Another repository's practice text, resolved into this tree at session
# start by tools/precedent_session_practices.py and rebuilt every time.
# NEVER COMMIT IT. It holds the universal catalogue's prose, which lives in
# alex137/BestPractice and is merely read here; committing a copy is exactly
# the drift the untracked-file design exists to prevent (upstream calls the
# committed variant "shape 2" and rejected it). Measured before this line
# existed: `git check-ignore` said not ignored, so the generated file was
# offered to the next `git add -A`.
.precedent/
